# Design tokens

App UI must use the Aeryo token system. Do not put raw hex, `rgb()`, `rgba()`, `hsl()`, or `oklch()` in component props, `style={{}}`, or local constants.

Tokens live in `src/design-system/tokens/` and are wired through `src/design-system/theme/`. ESLint (`no-restricted-syntax` in `eslint.config.mjs`) fails the build on hardcoded hex in `src/`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Box bg="#0B0F14" />
<Box style={{ color: "rgb(11, 15, 20)" }} />

// ✅ GOOD — semantic (theme-aware light/dark)
<Box bg="bg" color="fg" />

// ✅ GOOD — raw palette, when the surface is NOT theme-aware
// (full-bleed photo screens that stay dark in both modes)
<Box bg="ink.950" color="white" />
```

If the color you need is missing, add it in `src/design-system/tokens/colors.ts` (and a semantic token in `semantic-tokens.ts` if it has a role). Do not invent a one-off hex in the component.

Do not use Chakra's unthemed palettes (`gray`, `red`, `orange`, `whiteAlpha`, …). Use `teal` (the one primary), `danger`/`caution`/`success` for status, `ink.*` for neutrals, `lime` only for wind data.
